# CODEOWNERS — the files a pull request may not merge without the owner having opened them.
#
# Written 2026-09-21, findings A3 / A6 / SEC-4 / A9. Every path here is one where a change that
# LOOKS harmless in a diff can loosen a rule, take a key, or reach every player: the contract an
# agent works under, the signed personas, the verbatim record of what the owner said, the deploy
# recipe, the public shell, and the one page that holds the owner's Issues token.
#
# This file does nothing by itself. It takes effect when the owner turns on "Require review from
# Code Owners" in a ruleset on main (docs/SECURITY.md). With exactly one human on the repo that rule
# is set with the owner as a bypass actor: it stops a second agent's PR merging on green alone, and
# it does not stop the owner merging his own. test/leaves.js keeps every path here real.

# EVERYTHING, first — so no two non-owner accounts can satisfy the review rule for each other on a
# path this file forgot (the critic's finding 5, 2026-09-21). The lines below name WHY each path
# matters; this one line is the lock.
